{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Can she forget.</b> Because HaShem planted in the nature of all females compassion for their children, He spoke thus." "<b>Nursling.</b> Like עולל, and likewise עול ימים וזקן (Isaiah 65:20)." "<b>Has compassion on the son of her womb.</b> The meaning is doubled." "<b>Even these may forget.</b> There are also cruel women who forget their children, and it is possible that these will forget." "<b>And I will not forget you.</b> And the reason for 'nursling' is that upon the small one she has more compassion, for he has no strength."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:46.067413308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}